      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ENGULF (10) didn't have much luck on debut at Ballarat when getting trapped away on the fence before getting home strongly late. Shouldered a handy price tag at the sales being a half sister to G1 Oakleigh Plate winner Shamal Wind (2015). Suspect she's got plenty of improvement to come and with even luck she can get off the mark this time. VESPERS (9) resumes. Her Pakenham placings last campaign and a recent jumpout here make her a genuine threat if forward enough. LONNEGAN (4) was thereabouts on debut at Echuca and has upside with the blinkers going on. SILVER LIGHTNING (2) has lacked a finishing effort in two runs back but strips fitter third-up and comes into calculations after some key outs.",
